// Chunked Gated DeltaNet (linear attention) scan -- matrix-core path.
//
// GENERATED by kdev/gen_gdn_chunk16.py --waves 2; edit the generator.
//
// One workgroup owns one (head, sequence) and 32 of the 128 state columns as
// 2 waves of 16. The state shard lives in registers -- 64 f32 per
// lane, lane L holding rows 4L..4L+3 of every column, so it loads and stores
// one f32x4 per column -- and is staged to LDS as f16 once per 16-token chunk.
//
// Per chunk a wave issues 8 WMMA for A = S^T K, 8 for B = S^T Q, 8 for the
// state update and 8 for its half of the shared G = K^T K / QK = K^T Q, then
// runs 16 scalar steps with no cross-lane traffic. The shipped scan runs two
// wave reductions per token.
//
// LDS 31808 B per workgroup, so two workgroups per CU.

